\] Notice that $(11 + \sqrt{37})(11 - \sqrt{37}) = 121 - 37 = 84$ and $(4 + \sqrt{37})(-4 + \sqrt{37}) = 37 - 16 = 21$. So, we have: \[
\text{Area} = \sqrt{84 \cdot 21} = \sqrt{1764} = 42
